  {:id :problem-probed-sound-before-the-frame,
   :text
   "NEW THIS FRAME, AND IT IS THE POINT. m93J06 was probed for soundness BEFORE registration, by codex-8 on branch probe/m93J06-soundness (commit 9ba574a6), in one dispatch. Ten witnesses compiled axiom-clean in problems/m93J06/lean/Soundness.lean: apm_m93j06_Solves and apm_m93j06_IsFlow each have an exhibited inhabitant AND an exhibited non-inhabitant (a predicate satisfied by everything is as defective as one satisfied by nothing - m99J06 would not have been caught by inhabitation alone); the all-of-R solution formulation is shown to permit genuine uniqueness, which is the m99J06 defect shape checked directly; and ContDiff occurs only as `ContDiff R 1`, never the analytic top. The frozen file was NOT modified (git diff --exit-code against the pin, exit 0) and no proof strategy was published - ground control checked both before this registration was written. This is the first frame whose problem was not a coin flip."}
  {:id :conjunct-4-pre-discharged,
   :text
   "DECLARED SO THE ANALYST DOES NOT OVER-CREDIT THE CLOSE. The fourth conjunct of apm_m93j06 - the negated Holder-uniqueness universal - is ALREADY PROVED in the frozen file at the pin: `apm_m93j06_not_holder_unique` sits at Main.lean:132, supported by apm_m93j06_zero_solves_sqrt and apm_m93j06_signedSquare_solves_sqrt. A solver discharges that conjunct by citing an existing lemma. m93J06 is therefore FOUR conjuncts of work, not five, and any comparison of its close against a five-conjunct problem is not like-for-like."}
  {:id :read-path-state-declared,
   :text
   "THE READ PATH IS PARTLY REPAIRED AND THE REMAINING DEFECT IS KNOWN AND UNFIXED. Fixed and live: the lexical query is now OR-joined (7b188d8c) rather than a conjunction, which is what let f13 return anything at all - measured, `hilbert weak-convergence computes` scoped returns 0 and the OR form returns 25. NOT on the path despite being merged: 6bfe5808 (document frequencies scoped to the memory population) runs only inside query-anchor-term-memory-df, which executes only under --anchor-source memory-df; the default is :problem-idf and this frame does not flip it. Also not on the path: anchor-df-band [3 150]. UNFIXED (D60): default-query-term-limit is 4 and the three-source round-robin truncates one slot before the distinctive terms, while text-keywords orders each source by PROBLEM-CORPUS IDF, which against a corpus of mathematics ranks prose words rarest. f13's issued query was `finding OR equality OR clause OR strong` while the extractor had found sobolev, galerkin, riesz and inner_eq. Expect the lexical route to underperform and the pattern cascade to carry most of the load; f13 surfaced five memories of which exactly one arrived by :content-match, ranked 27th of 30 in a seed where 27 hits were coordination chatter."}
  {:id :append-retry-live,
   :text
   "RESTART-TIME WRITE BEHAVIOUR CHANGED between frame 12 and this frame. futon3c evidence appends now RETRY on :store-unreachable with a 300s window (f1322302, c035df5c, 99176882, claude-11) instead of returning a SocialError immediately. Before this, README-fts.md section 7 was correct that an evidence write outage is LOSSY - no spool, no retry - and frames 9 through 12 ran under that condition. The 300s default is sized off measured stop-to-healthy times (42s and 61s on Zone). Any comparison of this frame against frames 9-12 on write-loss grounds is not like-for-like."}
  {:id :harness-moved-under-the-batch,
   :text
   "The harness has moved repeatedly and by other hands. Twelve defects were fixed between frame 10's close and the original batch registration (D1 D2 D3 D4 D5 D6 D7 D8 D9 D10 D24 D25); the recall read path changed after that (d893280a, 10937528, 7b188d8c, 6bfe5808); then three commits from another agent landed in src/ - f2cccbb0, 7b2d7cdd and 62bfc210 (local Codex identity in zone defaults, zone nick match, and enforce singular ownership of Codex sessions) - touching agency/registry.clj, agency/roster_store.clj, scripts/dev-zone-env and scripts/codex-picker, which is seat identity and session ownership, the machinery this frame's seats are dispatched through. The pin has since moved again to e1925203. Ground control authored and reviewed the read-path commits and NEITHER authored nor reviewed the session-ownership ones. Declared because a between-frame difference this large must not be discovered by the Analyst from a diff, and because a seat-identity or duplicate-session anomaly in this frame should look there first."}
  {:id :promotion-is-non-atomic,
   :text
   "KNOWN LIVE DEFECT, D62, declared so the frame does not lose work rediscovering it. promote-artifact posts the pattern attach and :proposed status BEFORE writing the review (memory_lifecycle.clj:333-340). A failure after the attach leaves the edge in exactly the state lines 321 and 328 refuse, permanently unpromotable by that path - three of frame 13's scribe memories are poisoned this way and readable in the store stuck at :proposed. Compounding it, the refusal receipt says only 'Tool execution failed' (D43), so a harmless pre-flight refusal and a destructive half-applied one read identically. f13-guide's evidence, offered as hypothesis and not proof: promotions 1-3 ran back to back in one shell loop and all failed after the attach; promotion 4 ran alone minutes later and went end to end. PROMOTE ONE AT A TIME, WITH A GAP."}
  {:id :dead-regime-pin,
   :text
   "STANDING SERIES DEFECT, FOUND BY f15-guide AT ITS ORIENTATION ACK. (:problem :regime) is the string e7b9ec02599b36845c68ca053416787a23ac29a8 and it resolves in NO repository - not apm-lean, not mathlib4, not futon3c. It is copied verbatim into all fourteen registrations in this series, so it has never anchored anything. Declared rather than silently corrected because every prior frame ran with it and a silent fix would make this frame incomparable to them. SEPARATELY, and this one is a vocabulary defect that has bitten: :lean-revision 4331becf IS valid but resolves only in /home/joe/code/mathlib4, while the apm-lean anchor is :reg/environment-revision a92ffb6c. The series has been calling both 'the pin'. Diff the frozen statement against a92ffb6c, or against the Main.lean blob 793cfe3b51305ee997c7ba60a17553633999063e."}],
