 [{:id :problem-closed-on-artifact,
   :text
   "ARTIFACT AXIS. m93J06 reaches zero executable sorries, axiom-clean, with the frozen statement mechanically unchanged — or its residual is strictly reduced and localised into named per-clause pieces. This is a claim about the Lean file and is settled by re-running the file: sorry count, `#print axioms`, and a diff of the frozen statement. Frames 9 and 10 each closed on the solver's FIRST dispatch, so this is a real prediction with a track record, not a formality."}
  {:id :problem-solved,
   :text
   "MATHEMATICS AXIS, AND IT IS THE ONE THAT COUNTS. The statement m93J06 closes is NON-VACUOUS: the objects it quantifies over are exhibited non-empty in at least one concrete case, so the close is a mathematical result and not a proof about an empty class. This is the objective the whole apparatus exists to serve — the corpus has ~207 open problems and the machine is being built to go through them. A frame that repairs its own plumbing and does not solve its problem has failed, however green its other measures read. SPLIT FROM :problem-closed AFTER f12 (ruling, 2026-08-19): f12 met every literal condition of the old single prediction — 0 sorries, axiom-clean, statement unchanged — while proving a vacuous statement, and the guide and the Analyst then adjudicated the SAME prediction to opposite verdicts because it silently conjoined two independent claims. Neither was wrong; the prediction was. Adjudicate the two axes separately and never collapse them: a frame may confirm the artifact axis and refute this one, and that PAIR is the finding, not a contradiction to be resolved. The frame disposition (:closed / :defective / :partial) MUST travel with any report of either axis — a verdict quoted without its disposition is not a permitted citation of this frame."}
  {:id :memory-contributes-to-close,
   :text
   "THE MEASUREMENT THIS FRAME EXISTS TO MAKE. A memory surfaced by recall is attested USED by the solver or the student, per-id, in its own words, and contributes to the close of a SOUND problem.\n\nTHE PRIOR IS ZERO, AND THIS IS A FIRST MEASUREMENT RATHER THAN A REPLICATION. Ruled 2026-08-19 by ground control after f15-guide found the contradiction at its orientation ack. Earlier registrations claimed \"f10 produced the series' first uncontaminated instance (the student derived its own conjunct from a route memory)\". That claim cannot stand against the persisted cycle state: a01J06 and m93J02 both record memory-use steps = 0 - not zero uses, NO memory-use instrumentation ran at all. Whatever was observed at f10 was a PROSE ATTRIBUTION by a reader, not an attested step, and the honest prior is therefore zero attested instances on a sound problem.\n\nThe only attested instance in the series is frame 13's, where the solver returned USED for two memories and IGNORED with reasons for three more - on a problem whose model was provably UNINHABITED. So what has been demonstrated is transfer of DEFECT-DETECTION, on a broken problem. Whether the same pipeline moves MATHEMATICS on a sound one is untested, and is what this frame asks.\n\nADJUDICATE AGAINST THE ATTESTATION AND NOTHING ELSE. Surfaced-and-unused is a real outcome and must be reported as one. A plausible coincidence between a memory's content and the solver's method is NOT evidence - frame 13 produced the most temptingly attributable coincidence in the series and was settled only by the solver's own per-id disposition. Do not infer use from resemblance.\n"}
  {:id :reviewed-attachment-gained,
   :text
   "SUPPORTING, NOT HEADLINE, AND QUALIFIED. The store gains at least ONE reviewed memory attachment. QUALIFIER, established by f11's guide from f9's actual promote-artifact args: an INDEPENDENTLY reviewed attachment is NOT reachable — that path needs a keyword :verdict the transport cannot express (D31). What IS reachable is attach-then-review with the GUIDE as reviewer of a STATUSLESS, PATTERNLESS deposit, which is exactly what f9 did (depositor f9-scribe, reviewer f9-guide, edge now :reviewed). So this predicts a GUIDE-reviewed attachment and must be adjudicated as such; a frame that gains one has NOT demonstrated independent review. Note the trap: attach-then-review REFUSES an edge already carrying a status or patterns (memory_lifecycle.clj:322,330), so a well-authored :proposed-with-patterns deposit is unpromotable while a patternless one is promotable. Good authoring forecloses the working route."}
  {:id :offer-disposition-populated,
   :text
   ":memory-disposition-offer-ids is NON-EMPTY, so runtime invariant F3 passes for the first time in a cascade-enabled frame. It was empty in f8, f9 and f10 because :write-use was unreachable from the conductor surface (D25), while all nine registrations from f2 to f10 declared :offer-use-disposition as a required capability. This is the capability becoming satisfiable rather than merely declared."}
  {:id :guidance-count-exact,
   :text
   "The recorded guidance count EQUALS the true number of guidance bells sent, and in particular is 0 if none were sent. D2 (73a6b0c2) is loaded from this frame onward. Before it, the subtrahend counted the flattened per-memory offer list rather than dispatch openings: f9 read -100 and f10 -101 with huge offer counts, and f11 read +1 with ZERO offers because the subtrahend then failed to cancel the solver dispatch. Same defect, both signs. This is the first frame that can test the fix live, so a wrong value here means the repair did not reach the running image."}
  {:id :scribe-card-pinned-resolves,
   :text
   "The machine injects the card this registration PINS, resolved by blob, with no guide declaring it authoritative by hand. D8 (ca0f297e) is loaded from this frame onward; f8, f9, f10 and f11 all papered over conductor.clj's hardcoded scribe.md, and f11 saw the pre-fix constant injected twice in one cycle. Like :guidance-count-exact this tests whether a source fix reached the running image, which is the D30 failure this batch is sequenced to avoid."}
  {:id :student-memory-promotable,
   :text
   "If the student records a memory, it is NOT refused on domain grounds. f10's e-3a3aed11 was unpromotable because frame students recorded under :domain :zaif-work against a :mathematics pin (D5). This is conditional on the student choosing to record: a frame where it records nothing neither confirms nor refutes, and must be reported as inapplicable rather than as a pass."}
  {:id :cascade-seeds-from-recall,
   :text
   "Offers are seeded from patterns attached to RECALL-SURFACED memories, not from the problem's own touch-set. f10 refuted the opposite premise decisively: it was chosen for touching no @why-edged pattern and produced 48 :why-hop offers via math-strategy/missing-dependency-protocol. This frame states the corrected mechanism as the prediction, so it is tested rather than assumed."}
  {:id :refusals-are-traceable,
   :text
   "Any conductor action refused during this frame appears in the emitted trace as an :action-refusals receipt. In f10 three promotion refusals existed ONLY in the guide's prose report and the machine trace was consistent with a clean run (D6, fixed 585a980e). If nothing is refused this frame the prediction is inapplicable, not confirmed — say so."}
  {:id :analyst-survives-two-frames,
   :text
   "analyst-3 completes duties A, B and F at this close. It is at TENURE 1 OF 2 and therefore does NOT owe succession here — the handoff document, memory-surface pointer and W-entry fall due at frame 16, its second and last. SCOPE THIS CAREFULLY WHEN ADJUDICATING: the preceding registration's copy of this text said the analyst executes its succession AT THIS CLOSE, which was true of the previous analyst at frame 12 and is false here. That text shipped UNADJUDICABLE in frame 13 (D56) and was caught a THIRD time by gen-registration.bb before this frame opened. A prediction that cannot be satisfied or refuted by the frame it ships in is a defect in the prediction, not a result — report it as such if you meet one.\n"}],
